# AlphaLN Shadow-Twin Isolation

AlphaLN is a shadow research twin of Little Nate. It exists so we can experiment
with clinical coevolution loops (self-play patient sims, DPO exports, promotion
gates, etc.) without touching the live ANI ("Little Nate") that clients talk to.

These invariants are **security- and privacy-critical**. Do not weaken any of
them without an explicit, dated approval from the user.

## Invariant 1 — AlphaLN never speaks to a client

- The only ingress path is the admin console at `/api/admin/alphaln/*`.
- The router uses `require_admin` **and** a body-level `_require_dr_nevedal1`
  check. No coach, no other admin, and no client can reach it.
- There is no WebSocket, Twilio, or bridge path that instantiates AlphaLN. If a
  new path is added, it MUST route through `nate_inference_router` under the
  normal "Little Nate" identity — never as `AlphaLN`.

## Invariant 2 — AlphaLN never writes to production memory

AlphaLN turns live in dedicated tables (migrations 421–428):

| Table | Migration | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `alphaln_conversations` | 421 | admin twin sessions |
| `alphaln_messages` | 421 | turn-by-turn transcript |
| `alphaln_shadow_observations` | 422 | de-identified scores of live LN replies (Slice 3) |
| `alphaln_gym_runs` | 423 | admin-triggered bakeoff audit (Slice 5) |
| `alphaln_trajectory_runs` / `alphaln_trajectory_nodes` | 424 | MCTS skeleton (Slice 6) |
| `alphaln_sensor_joins` | 425 | biometric ingest schema only, no writes yet (Slice 7) |
| `alphaln_promotion_candidates` | 426 | paved-and-locked promotion ledger (Slice 8) |
| `alphaln_pack_drafts` | 428 | CI pack specs; human accept required before drip can see them |

AlphaLN code MUST NOT write to any of these production surfaces:

- `conversation_history`
- `nate_intelligence_crystals`
- `nevedal_metrics`
- `nevedal_metrics_v2`
- `pmb_reports_*`
- `sensitive_bridge_*`
- `outcome_envelope` (pack drafts never mint fuel rows; drip stays unused-only)

If a future slice wants to reuse memory, it goes through a **read-only** view
of the production tables, not a write path.

## Invariant 3 — Feature-flagged and dark by default

- Backend gate: `ENABLE_ALPHALN_TWIN` (default false). When false, every
  `/api/admin/alphaln/*` endpoint returns `503 AlphaLN twin disabled`.
- UI gate: the AlphaLN nav tab in `dashboard/command.html` is
  `display:none` unless `sessionStorage.getItem('username') === 'DrNevedal1'`.
  This is a UX hint only — the server gate is authoritative.

## Invariant 4 — Same PII controls as the rest of Nate

- Every admin prompt is passed through `maybe_pseudonymize_prompt` before it
  reaches `NateInferenceRouter`.
- The provider's reply is passed through `restore_text(book)` before it is
  written to `alphaln_messages` or returned to the admin.
- MFA freshness is enforced (`enforce_mfa_recent`) on all mutating endpoints
  (session create, message send, session end).

## Invariant 5 — Additive schema only

Migration 421 is additive. Never `ALTER TABLE` on `alphaln_conversations` or
`alphaln_messages` in a hotfix — cut a new migration. Never drop these tables;
they are the audit trail for a shadow research surface.

## Invariant 6 — Never merge AlphaLN weights into ANI without a human gate

If a later slice wires an auto-promotion pipeline from AlphaLN to Little Nate,
`nate_clinical_flags.auto_promote_enabled()` MUST stay `False` in code and
require a human review step before any weight/PEFT change is served to a
client. AlphaLN's job is to *propose*; only the admin promotes.

## Invariant 7 — Isolation is testable

Any change to the AlphaLN surface must keep the offline tests in
`backend/tests/test_alphaln_admin_api.py` green, including:

- flag-off → 503 on every endpoint
- non-admin → 403
- admin but not `DrNevedal1` → 403
- happy path: create session → send message → read transcript → end session
- rate limit trips after `_MSG_RATE_MAX` sends inside `_MSG_RATE_WINDOW_S`
- Slices 3–8 endpoints (`observations`, `gym/*`, `trajectory/*`,
  `promotion/*`) and pack-drafts (`pack-drafts/*`) return 503 when
  `ENABLE_ALPHALN_TWIN` is off

## Invariant 8 — Shadow observer never writes back

The `AlphaLNShadowObserver` (Slice 3) reads `conversation_history` READ-ONLY.
It MUST NOT UPDATE, DELETE, or INSERT into any production table. Its only
write target is `alphaln_shadow_observations`. `user_id` values are stored
as HMAC pseudonyms via `ALPHALN_OBSERVER_SALT`; raw usernames or hardware IDs
must never land in that table.

## Invariant 9 — Trajectory search is a stub until wired

`alphaln_trajectory_search.execute_run` returns `not_implemented` unless
BOTH `ENABLE_ALPHALN_TRAJECTORY_SEARCH` is on AND
`app.state.alphaln_trajectory_engine` is a callable. Any future engine MUST
NOT call live PMB/clinical bridges, MUST NOT read raw usernames, and MUST
operate against reactive-patient sims only.

## Invariant 10 — Sensor joins are consent-gated

`alphaln_sensor_joins` (migration 425) is schema-only in Slice 7. Any future
ingester MUST check `users.biometrics_disabled = false` AND populate
`consent_receipt_id` from `biometric_consent_receipts` before insert. No
back-fill from historical audio, no simulated data.

## Invariant 11 — Promotion is human-gated

`alphaln_promotion.assert_auto_promote_locked()` runs on every
`/api/admin/alphaln/promotion/*/review` call. If it ever throws, treat that
as a P0 incident: the auto-promote code path leaked into `True`. Approving a
candidate marks the row `approved`; it does NOT touch the inference router or
crystal tables. A human operator must promote out-of-band.

## Invariant 12 — AlphaLN does not affect the sovereign trust score

`alphaln_auditor.AlphaLNAuditor` is log-only. There is no row for AlphaLN in
`trust_baseline` and none of the 29 trust auditors should be extended to
score AlphaLN endpoints until this rule is amended. AlphaLN health lives at
`/api/admin/alphaln/health` and in container logs — never in the sovereign
trust report.

## Invariant 13 — Pack drafts never auto-fuel

`alphaln_pack_drafts` stores specs only. `generate` writes draft rows.
`review` with `accepted` materializes `catalog_aln_*` under the writable
packs root. It MUST NOT call `run_fuel_volume_burst`, drip, or INSERT
`outcome_envelope`. Replay stays CEO-only.
